# DIAGNOSTICS

When a program can't be linked, `Process.start` throws, and the starter prints `process start:` and why, naming the object: a library bootfs's `lib/` doesn't have, another build of a library than the one an object was linked against (`NAME was linked against another build of LIB`), an undefined symbol, a relocation type that isn't supported, or general-dynamic TLS.

# BUGS

An object linked without the note is not checked.
A program pushed to the launcher (vx-reload(1)) can't need libraries: it is in neither a bootfs image nor a namespace.
Every library is loaded and relocated again at each start, its writable pages copied: starting a Kit app takes milliseconds, a static program's tens of microseconds.
